hromaggus/drunkgoat/","guild":"Illidans Highbourne","race":"Blood Elf","class":"Paladin","player_class_enum":"PALADIN","blizzard_post_count":"10","level":"80","achievement_points":"28280"},"post_url":"/t/pass-does-not-work/294535/3","alias_avatar":"https://render.worldofwarcraft.com/eu/character/chromaggus/213/101754837-avatar.jpg?alt=/wow/static/images/2d/avatar/10-1.jpg","alias_username":"Drunkgoat-chromaggus","poster_alias":{"alias":{"name":"Drunkgoat-chromaggus","avatar":"https://render.worldofwarcraft.com/eu/character/chromaggus/213/101754837-avatar.jpg?alt=/wow/static/images/2d/avatar/10-1.jpg","url":"https://worldofwarcraft.com/en-gb/character/eu/chromaggus/drunkgoat/","user_id":201899,"id":89818,"selected":true,"post_count":10,"alias_custom_fields":[{"name":"profile_url","value":"https://worldofwarcraft.com/en-gb/character/eu/chromaggus/drunkgoat/"},{"name":"realm","value":"Chromaggus"},{"name":"achievement_points","value":"28280"},{"name":"level","value":"80"},{"name":"race","value":"Blood Elf"},{"name":"player_class","value":"Paladin"},{"name":"player_class_enum","value":"PALADIN"},{"name":"classic","value":"f"},{"name":"guild","value":"Illidans Highbourne"}]}},"reply_to_alias":{"id":79599,"username":"Gráinne-earthen-ring","name":"Gráinne","avatar_template":"https://render.worldofwarcraft.com/eu/character/earthen-ring/234/158434538-avatar.jpg?alt=/wow/static/images/2d/avatar/4-1.jpg"},"animated_avatar":null,"user_post_count":10,"character":{"name":"GurliGebis","guild":"Illidans Highbourne","achievement_points":"28280","level":"80","class":"Paladin","race":"Blood Elf","player_class_enum":"PALADIN","classic":false},"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":3270412,"name":"Palabra","username":"Palabra-11710","avatar_template":"/en/wow/plugins/discourse-blizzard-plugin/images/avatars/wow/default.png","created_at":"2021-07-05T08:54:18.142Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIt’s a really nasty glitch, and seeing it from get go is just devastating enough to get lost easily. Thanks to Lazey for sharing the issue back on PTR!\u003cbr\u003e\nI thought I would showcase several things that can happen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe basic issue is just as mentioned:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cem\u003eWhen a faster creature performs a round of no action – that is passes or swaps – the other side is unable to act.\u003c/em\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n(Certain „ idle” multiple round effects are affected, but not the other. The rule of thumb seems to be, that if an ability doesn’t have „ X Round Ability” in the tooltip, such as \u003cem\u003eEmerald Dream\u003c/em\u003e, \u003cem\u003eHibernate\u003c/em\u003e, \u003cem\u003ePuppies of the Flame\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003eSons of the Root\u003c/em\u003e, it is affected and will skip rounds to the detriment of slower opponents.)\u003cbr\u003e\nThere is also one more thing, about it soon.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLog no. 1: The Stuff Itself\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nAldrussian Sproutling ❱❱❱ Manos\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cem\u003eA couple rounds of passing, with swapping at the end, and «Photosynthesis» thrown in to show that casting healing still constitues an action, but not events over time.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nExpand\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003eRound 1\nRound 2\nRound 3\nRound 4\n[Photosynthesis] applied [Photosynthesis] to your Aldrusian Sproutling.\n[Arcane Storm] dealt 112 damage to your Aldrusian Sproutling.\n[Arcane Storm] dealt 112 damage to your Qiraji Guardling.\n[Arcane Storm] dealt 112 damage to your Blazehound.\n[Arcane Storm] changed the weather to [Arcane Winds].\n[Photosynthesis] healed 84 damage from your Aldrusian Sproutling.\nRound 5\n[Photosynthesis] healed 28 damage from your Aldrusian Sproutling.\nRound 6\n[Photosynthesis] healed 0 damage from your Aldrusian Sproutling.\nRound 7\nBlazehound is now your active pet.\n[Photosynthesis] healed 0 damage from your Aldrusian Sproutling.\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLog no. 2: The Equal Speed:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nBlazehound (276) = Manos\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cem\u003eThis hottie just passed all along. When the speed is equal, the glitch still happens if the creature is rolled to “act” first that round. Thus this bug “knows” the acting order even if attacks such as «Alpha Strike» don’t, but I digress.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nExpand\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003eRound 8\n[Photosynthesis] healed 0 damage from your Aldrusian Sproutling.\nRound 9\n[Mana Surge] dealt 397 damage to your Blazehound.\n[Mana Surge] dealt 140 damage to your Blazehound.\n[Photosynthesis] healed 0 damage from your Aldrusian Sproutling.\n[Photosynthesis] fades from your Aldrusian Sproutling.\nRound 10\nRound 11\n[Mana Surge] dealt 411 damage to your Blazehound.\n[Mana Surge] dealt 140 damage to your Blazehound.\nRound 12\n[Mana Surge] dealt 325 damage to your Blazehound.\nYour Blazehound died.\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd now there’s the kick: even though normally interrupted multi-round abilities don’t continue later, this is not the case there. The following hits of \u003cem\u003eMana Surge\u003c/em\u003e eventually do happen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLog no. 3: Stun with a Swap\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nQiraji Guardling (260) ❰❰❰ Manos\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cem\u003eWhen you stun an enemy, what they’re supposed to do? Why, they can either swap or pass! And what happens when the stunned one is faster? The round is glitched against you.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nExpand\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003e[Arcane Winds] is no longer the weather.\n[Sandstorm] changed the weather to [Sandstorm].\n[Recovery] healed 56 damage from your Qiraji Guardling.\nRound 2\n[Mana Surge] dealt 216 damage to your Qiraji Guardling.\n[Blackout Kick] applied [Stunned] to enemy Manos.\n[Magic] fades from enemy Manos.\nRound 3 (Manos swaps)\nHanos is now enemy active pet.\n[Stunned] fades from enemy Manos.\n[Stunned] applied [Resilient] to enemy Manos.\nRound 4\n[Crush] dealt 209 damage to enemy Hanos.\n[Flash] dealt 74 damage to your Qiraji Guardling.\n[Flash] applied [Partially Blinded] to your Qiraji Guardling.\n[Recovery] healed 56 damage from your Qiraji Guardling.\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut wait, there’s more!\u003cbr\u003e\nUsually the \u003cem\u003eCrush\u003c/em\u003e would hit Hanos at the round 3, but it doesn’t because the round is busted. What about that round 4 though? Had I just clicked it that round? No. It’s the strike I had ordered at round 3 – similar to the postponed MS – that seems to happen automatically once my side’s regained the control. Or has it?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLog no. 4: Stun with a Pass\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nGrumpling (236) ❰❰❰ Fatos (\u0026amp; two debuffs counterweighting each other)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003e\nExpand\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003eRound 15\n[Arcane Slash] dealt 452 damage to your Grumpling.\n[Deep Freeze] dealt 396 damage to enemy Fatos.\n[Deep Freeze] applied [Stunned] to enemy Fatos.\n[Recovery] healed 57 damage from your Grumpling.\nRound 16 (Fatos passes)\n[Frost Shock] fades from enemy Fatos.\n[Stunned] fades from enemy Fatos.\n[Stunned] applied [Resilient] to enemy Fatos.\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSimilarly to the case before, a \u003cem\u003eSnowball\u003c/em\u003e scheduled for round 16 happened at round 17 automatically. If such an ability is on cooldown, it will happen aswell, looking as if it ignored the cooldown.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat’s all from me! Hopefully even without a few more multi-round moves, that’s enough to cover any case you might have observed. If not, feel free to ask questions, while attaching the log of the fight.\u003cbr\u003e\nYou can use PetBattleLogKeeper to save logs within a text-friendly background.\u003cbr\u003e\n(To attach a link to an image without a forum rank, use preformatted text. I’d advise Discord or Imgur for hosting.)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2021-07-05T11:06:14.780Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":146,"reads":21,"readers_count":20,"score":779.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":294535,"topic_slug":"pass-does-not-work","display_username":"Palabra","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":9,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":11710,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"user_custom_fields":{"guild":"A Dancing Paladin","race":"Dwarf","class":"Paladin","player_class_enum":"PALADIN","profile_url":"https://worldofwarcraft.com/en-gb/character/eu/burning-legion/remte/","classic":"t","level":"25","achievement_points":"29110","blizzard_post_count":"129"},"post_url":"/t/pass-does-not-work/294535/4","alias_avatar":"https://render.worldofwarcraft.com/eu/character/burning-legion/176/119841456-avatar.jpg?alt=/wow/static/images/2d/avatar/3-1.jpg","alias_username":"Remte-burning-legion","poster_alias":{"alias":{"name":"Remte-burning-legion","avatar":"https://render.worldofwarcraft.c